{
  "id": "universal-dash-dance",
  "name": "Dash dance",
  "part": "tech",
  "characters": "all",
  "goal": "Dash back and forth without breaking into a run",
  "why": "A dash can be turned around in one frame; a run cannot. Dashing back and forth keeps {char} moving in and out of the opponent's range while every option stays open: from any dash {char} can dash the other way, jump, shield or attack.",
  "tutorial": {
    "camera": {
      "follow": "player",
      "distance": 140,
      "height": 10
    },
    "what": "A dash dance is a dash turned around before it becomes a run, again and again. Each reversal costs one frame of turn.",
    "expect": "Each dance is judged when {char} stops or starts to run: how many dashes back, and whether a dash became a run. After misses, the coach shows the dashes and turns frame by frame.",
    "example": [
      {
        "stick": [
          1,
          0
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 4
      },
      {
        "stick": [
          -1,
          0
        ],
        "frame": 5,
        "hold": 5
      },
      {
        "stick": [
          1,
          0
        ],
        "frame": 10,
        "hold": 5
      },
      {
        "stick": [
          -1,
          0
        ],
        "frame": 15,
        "hold": 5
      },
      {
        "stick": [
          1,
          0
        ],
        "frame": 20,
        "hold": 5
      }
    ],
    "marks": {
      "1": "Frame 1: stick to the side. Dash",
      "5": "Frame 5: stick the other way. One frame of turn",
      "6": "Frame 6: dash back",
      "10": "Frame 10: turn",
      "15": "Frame 15: turn",
      "20": "Frame 20: turn",
      "25": "Frame 25: stick let go. The last dash plays out"
    },
    "lessons": [
      {
        "title": "The dash and the run",
        "text": [
          "Smash the control stick to the side and {char} dashes. The stick has to pass 0.8 of its range within 2 frames of leaving the center; pushed slower, {char} walks.",
          "{char}'s initial dash is {DASH} frames. If the stick is still held forward on frame {DASH+1}, the dash becomes a run. Turned or let go by then, it stays a dash: let go, it plays out and {char} stands."
        ],
        "show": {
          "example": {
            "inputs": [
              {
                "stick": [
                  1,
                  0
                ],
                "frame": 1,
                "hold": "DASH+8"
              }
            ],
            "marks": {
              "1": "Frame 1: stick smashed to the side. Dash",
              "DASH": "Frame {DASH}: the last frame of the initial dash",
              "DASH+1": "Frame {DASH+1}: stick still held. Run"
            },
            "cues": [
              {
                "frames": [
                  1,
                  "DASH"
                ],
                "words": "Initial dash: {DASH} frames",
                "kind": "info"
              },
              {
                "frames": [
                  "DASH+1",
                  "DASH+8"
                ],
                "words": "Still held: a run",
                "kind": "late"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Dash back",
        "text": [
          "During the dash, smash the stick the other way. {char} turns for one frame, and if the stick is still past 0.8 on the next frame, {char} dashes the other way.",
          "A dash from standing ignores the stick for its first 4 frames, so turn it from frame 5 to frame {DASH+1}. A dash out of a turn can be turned again from its second frame, until its own frame {DASH+1}. A run turns around slowly."
        ],
        "show": {
          "example": {
            "inputs": [
              {
                "stick": [
                  1,
                  0
                ],
                "frame": 1,
                "hold": 4
              },
              {
                "stick": [
                  -1,
                  0
                ],
                "frame": 5,
                "hold": 5
              },
              {
                "stick": [
                  1,
                  0
                ],
                "frame": 10,
                "hold": 5
              }
            ],
            "marks": {
              "1": "Frame 1: dash",
              "4": "Frame 4: the last frame that ignores the stick",
              "5": "Frame 5: stick the other way. One frame of turn",
              "6": "Frame 6: stick still held. Dash back",
              "10": "Frame 10: turn",
              "11": "Frame 11: dash"
            },
            "cues": [
              {
                "frames": [
                  1,
                  4
                ],
                "words": "First 4 frames: turning is ignored",
                "kind": "info"
              },
              {
                "frames": [
                  5,
                  5
                ],
                "words": "Turn",
                "kind": "go"
              },
              {
                "frames": [
                  6,
                  9
                ],
                "words": "Dash back",
                "kind": "info"
              },
              {
                "frames": [
                  10,
                  10
                ],
                "words": "Turn",
                "kind": "go"
              },
              {
                "frames": [
                  11,
                  20
                ],
                "words": "Dash",
                "kind": "info"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "On the stage",
      "stage": "final-destination",
      "player": {
        "x": -20
      },
      "opponent": "none",
      "camera": {
        "follow": "player",
        "distance": 220,
        "height": 10
      }
    }
  ],
  "attempt": {
    "start": {
      "enters": "dash"
    },
    "judge": [
      {
        "enters": "wait"
      },
      {
        "enters": "run"
      }
    ],
    "cancel": [
      {
        "enters": "jump_squat"
      },
      {
        "enters": "shield"
      },
      {
        "enters": "dash_grab"
      }
    ],
    "limit": 300
  },
  "measures": {
    "ran": {
      "happened": {
        "enters": "run"
      }
    },
    "backs": {
      "count": {
        "enters": "dash",
        "from": "turn"
      }
    }
  },
  "verdict": {
    "success": "Dash dance without a run. Dashes back: {backs}."
  },
  "checks": {
    "no run": {
      "measure": "ran",
      "equals": false,
      "expect": "No run",
      "words": "the dash became a run",
      "headline": "Ran",
      "fix": "Turn the dash or let go of the stick by its frame {DASH+1}. Still held forward on that frame, the dash becomes a run, and a run turns around slowly."
    },
    "dashed back": {
      "measure": "backs",
      "at_least": 1,
      "expect": "A dash back",
      "words": "{char} never dashed the other way",
      "headline": "No dash back",
      "fix": "Smash the stick the other way on a frame from the dash's 5th to its {DASH+1}th, and keep it there one more frame: the first frame turns {char}, the second starts the dash back. A dash from standing ignores the stick for its first 4 frames."
    },
    "four": {
      "measure": "backs",
      "at_least": 4,
      "expect": "Four dashes back",
      "words": "{measure} dashes back",
      "headline": "Stopped early",
      "fix": "Keep turning each dash before it becomes a run, four times or more before you let go of the stick."
    }
  },
  "parts": [
    {
      "name": "The dash",
      "teach": "Smash the stick to the side to dash, then let go before frame {DASH+1}: {char}'s initial dash is {DASH} frames. The dash plays out and {char} stands.",
      "example": [
        {
          "stick": [
            1,
            0
          ],
          "frame": 1,
          "hold": 6
        }
      ],
      "marks": {
        "1": "Frame 1: stick to the side. Dash",
        "6": "Frame 6: stick let go",
        "7": "The dash plays out: no run"
      },
      "checks": [
        "no run"
      ],
      "success": "Dash without a run.",
      "streak": 3,
      "coach": {
        "rows": [
          {
            "label": "Dash",
            "state": "dash",
            "held": true,
            "perfect": [
              1
            ],
            "window": [
              1,
              "DASH"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Run",
            "state": "run",
            "perfect": []
          }
        ],
        "note": "{char}'s initial dash is {DASH} frames: let go of the stick or turn by frame {DASH+1}."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Dash back",
      "teach": "Dash, then smash the stick the other way on a frame from 5 to {DASH+1} and hold it: one frame of turn, then a dash back.",
